    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1307">

                <pb facs="1570" n="1372" xml:id="pg1372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1307<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the Interim
                        Committee</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-21">21 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">War</hi> 35987.
                    Secretary of War
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eyes Only</hi>
                    TopSec from Harrison.</p>
                <p>All your local military advisors engaged in preparation definitely favor your pet
                        city<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1307-f1"/> and would like to feel free to use it
                    as first choice if those on the ride select it out of four possible spots in the
                    light of local conditions at the time.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1307-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1307-f1-content">
                <p>The reference is to the selection of Kyoto as a possible target for atomic
                    attack. See Stimson and Bundy, <hi rendition="#italic">On Active
                        Service in Peace and War</hi>, p. 625.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
